      "id": "msg_05a6dae68e44ad8a016af7b79012e087d19f28fd8c5eed1f3d",
      "content": [
        {
          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"version\":\"design_judgment_v1\",\"case_key\":\"ddd2f5a8191c1ae70b57ec33\",\"status\":\"scored\",\"units\":[{\"unit_id\":\"task_requirements\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Required: the No Service request triggers customer identification and cellular-service diagnosis before a justified exit.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0004\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"}],\"rationale\":\"Identify the customer, obtain device-grounded diagnostics, address a missing SIM if reported, and apply the locked-SIM escalation rule if that condition becomes visible. The seeded faults are not facts available to the agent without discovery.\",\"applicability\":\"required\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":2,\"tool_use\":2,\"information\":2}},{\"unit_id\":\"reference_001\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Selected conditional: transfer is the intended exit once the SIM lock establishes that the issue cannot be solved with the available actions.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0314\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0564\"}],\"rationale\":\"After confirming the lock, call the transfer tool with an issue summary, then give the prescribed transfer message. The reference call alone does not justify transferring before diagnosis.\",\"applicability\":\"selected_conditional\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":1,\"tool_use\":1,\"information\":1}}],\"dimensions\":{\"workload\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"The sufficient path has several stages: identify the customer, diagnose the device, guide any needed preliminary fix, then transfer when the locked SIM is established. On a defensible path, a missing-SIM finding leads to reseating before a subsequent check reveals the lock. Payment, line resumption and APN repair are excluded after that decisive exit; seeded setup operations are not agent work.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0011\"}]},\"reasoning\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"The agent must distinguish a fixable missing SIM from a locked SIM requiring escalation, while avoiding an unsupported immediate transfer or charging every seeded fault to the path.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0027\"}]},\"tool_use\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"The path selects a phone-number customer lookup and coordinates user-side diagnostic or fix tools with the assistant-side transfer tool; arguments are ordinary rather than complex nested bindings.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0322\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0489\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0523\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0434\"}]},\"dependencies\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"Identification precedes technical support; a missing SIM may need reseating before a later SIM check exposes the decisive lock. Transfer depends on that finding and is followed by the prescribed message. No payment or other repairs are prerequisites to locked-SIM escalation.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0563\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0564\"}]},\"information\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"The agent has a phone number but must retrieve customer and device status; judge-only setup indicates possible overlapping causes but is not agent knowledge. This is ordinary staged verification, not a requirement to reconcile every account and device fault.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0370\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0206\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0011\"}]}},\"overall_score\":50,\"intended_endpoint\":{\"description\":\"A justified transfer to a human agent for SIM security while service remains unavailable, rather than restoration of signal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0310\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"}]},\"dependency_reasoning\":\"A sufficient diagnostic order is phone-number identification, initial service/status check, correction of airplane mode if found, SIM check, reseating if missing, and a repeat check that can establish the non-tool-fixable PIN lock. The lock is the decisive mandatory escalation condition; billing, APN and line repairs need not be completed afterward. Another diagnostic order could discover the lock earlier.\",\"score_rationale\":\"Ratings of 2 for workload, reasoning, tool use, dependencies and information yield 5 × 10 = 50. This reflects a staged diagnostic path to escalation, not a full repair of all seeded faults.\",\"uncertainties\":[\"The SIM-status tool's behavior after reseating a missing SIM that is also PIN-locked is not shown by an execution trace; the path is inferred from the setup definitions and policy.\",\"The broad instruction to try all possible resolutions before transfer is in tension with the specific instruction to escalate a locked SIM; the specific SIM-security exit governs this score.\",\"The scenario names `get_status_bar`, while the supplied user tool is `check_status_bar`; the documented cellular guide also uses `check_status_bar`.\"],\"source_quality_flags\":[\"Reference contains only the transfer call, omitting policy-required identification, diagnosis and transfer message.\",\"Scenario's `get_status_bar` example differs from the supplied `check_status_bar` tool name.\",\"Setup definitions and judge-only records describe intended state but were not executed or available as facts to the task agent.\"],\"unscorable_reason\":\"\"}",
          "type": "output_text",
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
